From c1cbf12dbb0d99a5bca62af8218edf841cf4e8cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vkd3d-crossover <noreply@vkd3d-crossover.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:12:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] feat: defer Metal render pipeline compilation

Problem: Freezes whenever the game needs a pipeline that is still being created.

Root cause: RE Engine re-creates its whole pipeline set (~48k render PSOs) on background threads every launch at ~16 ms each (~11 ms of it the Metal render pipeline compile), so the warm-up runs for minutes during play.

Fix: vkCreateGraphicsPipelines (plain non-multiview, non-tessellation, non-mesh path) builds the descriptor and hands the Metal compile to MVKDeferredPSOScheduler, which keeps 4 compiles in flight. The first use of a still-queued pipeline submits it ahead of the queue and waits for it alone; while a draw waits, no background compiles are submitted and shader-library compiles yield (at most 50 ms each). Compile failures surface at first use; draws without a pipeline state are skipped as before.

Verified by: Stutter shorter and rarer (user); 20 rendering/pipeline/multithread tests and psostress (8 threads x 300 PSOs) identical with deferral on and off.

Off switch: MVK_DEFERRED_PSO=0 (MVK_DEFERRED_PSO_INFLIGHT sets the concurrency, default 4)
